messages:
rachel: starting a small docs PR to add a JS quickstart for Optimize toolkit (focus: continuous batching + cache + quant profiles). would love a reviewer and a tiny runnable snippet. tagging @tom @nikhil

tom: nice — can you keep it under 20 lines and use the browser/Node SDK pattern? we should include a note about the recommended quant_profile for low-latency interactive apps.

rachel: yep planning a node snippet for SDK v0.8. will show batching config and an inline fallback policy.

nikhil: add a short test case in docs-ci that runs the snippet with a mock env so we catch runtime regressions. also watch the link anchors in the migration TOC (they changed last week).

amanda: small UX ask: include a one-sentence pointer about when NOT to use continuous batching (very low QPS single-request apps).

rachel: good call. here's a first draft of the snippet — please check copy/pasteability:

```javascript
// Node SDK v0.8 - continuous batching + cache + quant fallback
const { RedwoodClient } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new RedwoodClient();
(async () => {
  const res = await client.generate({
    model: 'optimize/interactive-v1',
    input: 'Short summary of last 2 messages',
    batching: { mode: 'continuous', batch_window_ms: 20, max_batch_tokens: 800 },
    cache: { enable_prefix_kv: true, ttl_seconds: 300 },
    quant_profile: 'latency-8bit',
    fallback: { on_high_contention: { quant_profile: 'compact-6bit' } }
  });
  console.log(res.text);
})();
```

nikhil: looks great. for docs-ci, suggest a miniature node-run job that sets REDWOOD_API_KEY=ci-test and runs the snippet with a mocked endpoint. i'll draft the workflow.

tom: runtime note: add a one-liner about warmup/priming so users know to prefill the cache if they expect long threads. also call out the minor token-count differences with 6bit profiles.

amanda: +1 on the warmup note. also please include an inline link to the quant-profile comparison chart (docs/optimize/quant-profiles) — but double-check anchor path before merging.

docs-bot: CI | docs-pr-4899: build failed - linkchecker: broken link in docs/optimize/migration-node.md: /optimize/quant-profiles#comparison

rachel: thanks bot — i mistakenly used the short anchor. will update to /optimize/quant-profiles#profile-comparison and push.

docs-bot: CI | docs-pr-4899: build passed \u2705

nikhil: pushed a docs-ci job draft to the branch: .github/workflows/docs-snippet-node.yml to run node snippet under mocked server.

amanda: reviewed wording and clarified the "when not to use" sentence. tiny nit about using "short-circuit fallback" phrasing.

tom: reviewed and left one inline suggestion on the fallback example (change compact-6bit -> compact-5bit for latency-first suggestion).

rachel: applied both suggestions, updated snippet, added warmup paragraph and the docs-ci workflow. merging after a quick final check. final URL: https://docs.redwood.ai/optimize/migration/node-quickstart

